<article class="env-definition" id="3E57E7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/3E57E7">Definition <span data-tag="3E57E7">5.4.2.5</span>.</a>accessible!functor If $\calC $ is an accessible $\infty $-category, then a functor $F: \calC \rightarrow \calC '$ is <em>accessible</em> if it is $\kappa $-continuous for some regular cardinal $\kappa $ (and therefore for all regular cardinals $\tau \geq \kappa $). </p>
